IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gva-dates`
IMPORT `gva-core`
IMPORT `gva-seat`

-- Graffiti Vandalism Act 2016 (WA) -- cases for the seat layer (gva-seat.l4): every exported question, for every role.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none:
-- the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). So these cases show both the answer and that the form never needs to ask those inputs.
-- The same device is used in the cases for the role a question is about, wherever the text says an input cannot
-- matter on those facts (the consent of the owner of one's own wall, the day obliterated when it has not been).
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the output. Days are counted under the
-- Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b): the first day is left out.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the seat layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked way` IS A `How the mark was applied`
ASSUME `an unasked kind` IS A `Kind of item`
ASSUME `an unasked notice position` IS A `The notice and me`
ASSUME `an unasked thing` IS A `Thing that may be forfeited`

`as the accused` MEANS `I put graffiti on property, or am accused of it`
`as the seller` MEANS `I sell spray paint or wide markers`
`as the owner or occupier` MEANS `I own or occupy property with graffiti on it`

`spraying` MEANS `by spraying, writing, drawing, marking or otherwise applying paint or another marking substance`
`etching` MEANS `by scratching or etching`
`a sticker` MEANS `in some other way, such as sticking on a poster or sticker`

`given to me, I own` MEANS `it was given to me, and I own the property`
`given to me, I occupy` MEANS `it was given to me, and I occupy the property but do not own it`
`given to me, I own and occupy` MEANS `it was given to me, and I both own and occupy the property`
`given to my occupier, I own` MEANS `it was given to the occupier, and I own the property`
`given to my owner, I occupy` MEANS `it was given to the owner, and I occupy the property but do not own it`
`no notice` MEANS `no notice has been given to me, or to the owner or occupier of my property`

